# Copy to .env (gitignored) to point this checkout at Postgres instead of the
# local SQLite file. Real environment variables always win over this file, and
# an empty value counts as unset, so a missing .env is fine.
#
# Postgres is used when any of these holds a postgres:// or postgresql:// URL:
#   PROG5_DATABASE_URL   - Prog5's own name for the setting
#   DATABASE_URL_POOLED  - pooled Neon connection (what a server should use)
#   DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED- direct Neon connection (migrations, bulk loads)
#   DATABASE_URL         - shared name, kept for compatibility
PROG5_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host-pooler.region.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
